From 83b5bd737d36ded8fa801d43cd2fe800da1a7ecc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:36:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Treasure Trails (beginner and easy) on the cache's cluehelper
 tables

Beginner and easy Treasure Trails driven by Jagex's own clue data, the
cluehelper_* dbtables in the cache (clue texts, npc/loc/coord targets, emotes,
outfits, STASH locs): Read opens trail_cluetext (or the map interface) with
the step; npc talks (anagrams, cryptics), Charlie the Tramp's item tasks,
Reldo's hot-cold strange device with its temperature readings, loc searches,
digs, and emote steps with Uri; Check steps; per-step scroll items for easy
(item param 623), swapped as the trail moves on; STASH units built from the
emote rows (Build, Search); the beginner and easy reward caskets rolled from
the OSRS Wiki tables into trail_rewardinv with the completion count message;
scroll boxes; ::clue [tier] [row|list] [steps left]. Small server-only tables
fill what the cache leaves out (Charlie's items, map interfaces, emote seqs,
casket tables).

NpcOpOverrides and LocOpOverrides let content take an npc or loc op ahead of
its own handler for the players it claims, so a clue step can take Talk-to or
Search on npcs and locs that already have content.
